Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/vishvananda/netlink v1.3.1

XfrmState gains ExtraAttrs, a list of XfrmAttr values, each a netlink
attribute type and its raw value, for attributes this package does not model.
The state writer, xfrmStateAddOrUpdate, appends each one unchanged and in
order directly after struct xfrm_usersa_info, before the attributes it writes
itself. The state reader, parseXfrmState, returns each attribute whose type is
above nl.XFRMA_MAX, with its own copy of the value. An attribute the package
defines but does not decode, such as XFRMA_LTIME_VAL, is not returned, so a
state read back and written again does not resend it.

Ze uses the hook to carry a private kernel attribute that only Ze's runtime
kernel implements, XFRMA_STATE_SCOPE (42): Ze's dataplane encodes it on a
state request and decodes it from a state dump
(internal/component/ike/dataplane/xfrm_state_scope_abi_linux.go). The hook
itself names no Ze concept and could be proposed upstream as a generic way to
carry an attribute the package does not know yet. No upstream pull request is
opened for it.

The appending is split out of xfrmStateAddOrUpdate as addXfrmExtraAttrs, so
that the request can be checked without sending it. Its test,
TestXfrmStateExtraAttributes in xfrm_state_extra_attrs_linux_test.go, checks
the attribute bytes written and the attributes read back, and passes
unprivileged.

Needs netlink-xfrm-09-icmp-flag.patch and the patches it needs: the
ExtraAttrs field follows the ICMP field of XfrmState that 09 adds.

Delete this patch when go.mod requires an upstream release that carries an
equivalent hook, and Ze's dataplane uses that instead.

